<title>USA: Sioux Falls hogs off $1.00-1.50 - USDA.</title>
<headline>Sioux Falls hogs off $1.00-1.50 - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>SIOUX FALLS 1997-05-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>USDA said barrows and gilts sold unevenly $1.00 to mostly $1.50 lower. Trading was slow. Top $58.00 per cwt.</p>
<p>    US 1-3    220-260 lbs   57.50-58.50, mostly 58.00</p>
<p>		  260-270 lbs   57.00-57.50</p>
<p>    US 2-3    270-280 lbs   56.00-57.00</p>
<p>		  280-290 lbs   55.00-56.00</p>
<p>    US 3-4    290-300 lbs   54.00-55.00</p>
<p>Sows - steady/up $1.00. Top $53.00.</p>
<p>    US 1-3    300-450 lbs    48.00-50.00</p>
<p>		  450-500 lbs    50.00-50.50</p>
<p>		  500-650 lbs    50.00-53.00, mostly 51.00-52.00</p>
</text>
